IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), PART VII.1, sections 152.13 to 152.2: payment of benefits (the maximum
-- number of weeks, the waiting period), the rate of weekly benefits and the family supplement, and the deductions
-- for earnings and for days on which the person is not entitled.
-- Piece ei5, written by the piece agent ei5 (Sonnet 5.5). Layer 1: from the Act's text alone, no point of view.
--
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars. Section 152.01(5) (keel rule `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest
-- dollar`) rounds an amount equal to a percentage or fraction of earnings or benefits to the nearest dollar, the higher
-- dollar when equidistant: it is applied to the result amounts (the rate, the maximum increase, the maximum rate, the
-- deduction of s 152.18(2) as a whole, the one fifth of s 152.19), never to a threshold that is only compared (fork F20).
-- The maximum yearly insurable earnings "as calculated under section 4" is a plain NUMBER input (the keel computes it
-- in `eia-core-maximum-earnings`; the published figure is outside the text). This module imports no other ei5 module.
-- What the Regulations decide is a plain input with "out of range: reg N (piece X)".
-- Dates: no enactment or commencement date in these sections.

§ `152.13 Benefits`

-- If a benefit period has been established, benefits may be paid for each week of unemployment that falls in it, subject to
-- the maximums of s 152.14 (so: while fewer weeks than the maximum for the reason have been paid).
-- src:2480 | 152.13 If a benefit period has been established for a self-employed person, benefits may be paid to the person for each week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period, subject to the maximums established by section 152.14.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.13 (src:2480)
GIVEN `a benefit period has been established for the self-employed person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the week is a week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks for which benefits have been paid for the reason` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks for the reason established by section 152.14` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.13 benefits may be paid for the week` IF
        `a benefit period has been established for the self-employed person`
    AND `the week is a week of unemployment that falls in the benefit period`
    AND `the number of weeks for which benefits have been paid for the reason` LESS THAN `the maximum number of weeks for the reason established by section 152.14`

§ `152.14 Maximum number of weeks`

-- Subsection (1): the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period (a) for pregnancy 15; (b) for the care of new-born or
-- adopted children, by the election under s 152.05, 35 or 61; (c) for a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine 26; (d) for
-- care or support of a family member 26; (e) of a critically ill child 35; (f) of a critically ill adult 15. The regular
-- reason is not a reason under this Part: NOTHING (not covered). Parental benefits with no election: NOTHING.
-- src:2482 | 152.14 (1) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits under this Part may be paid in a benefit period to a self-employed person
-- src:2483 | (a) because of pregnancy is 15;
-- src:2484 | (b) because the self-employed person is caring for one or more new-born children of the self-employed person, or one or more children placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption is, in accordance with the election under section 152.05,
-- src:2485 | (i) 35, or
-- src:2486 | (ii) 61;
-- src:2487 | (c) because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine is 26;
-- src:2488 | (d) because the person is providing care or support to one or more family members described in subsection 152.06(1) is 26;
-- src:2489 | (e) because the self-employed person is providing care or support to one or more critically ill children described in subsection 152.061(1), is 35; and
-- src:2490 | (f) because the self-employed person is providing care or support to one or more critically ill adults described in subsection 152.062(1) is 15.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(1) (src:2482-2490)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
      `the election made under section 152.05` IS A MAYBE `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.14(1) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` IS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `pregnancy` THEN JUST 15
    WHEN `caring for a new-born or adopted child` THEN
        CONSIDER `the election made under section 152.05`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST e THEN
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN JUST 35
            WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN JUST 61
    WHEN `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` THEN JUST 26
    WHEN `care or support of a family member` THEN JUST 26
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill child` THEN JUST 35
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill adult` THEN JUST 15

-- Subsection (2): for a single pregnancy 15; for the care of one or more children of a single pregnancy or placement, if the
-- election is the 35-week maximum, 35 or, if the weeks are divided under s 152.05, 40; if the 61-week maximum, 61 or 69.
-- Subsection (4) gives the same figures "under this Act" where a claim under this Part and a claim under s 23 are both made.
-- src:2492 | (2) The maximum number of weeks for which benefits under this Part may be paid
-- src:2493 | (a) for a single pregnancy is 15; and
-- src:2494 | (b) for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement is,
-- src:2495 | (i) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph (1)(b)(i), 35 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 152.05, 40, or
-- src:2496 | (ii) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), 61 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 152.05, 69.
-- src:2499 | Maximum — parental benefits
-- src:2500 | (4) If a claim is made under this Part in respect of a child or children referred to in paragraph (2)(b) and a claim is made under section 23 in respect of the same child or children, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of the child or children is,
-- src:2501 | (a) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph (1)(b)(i), 35 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 152.05, 40; or
-- src:2502 | (b) if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph (1)(b)(ii), 61 or, if the weeks for which benefits may be paid are divided in accordance with section 152.05, 69.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(2) and (4) (src:2492-2496) (src:2499-2502)
GIVEN `the maximum is for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made under section 152.05` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with section 152.05` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.14(2) and (4) the maximum number of weeks for a single pregnancy or placement` IS
    IF NOT (`the maximum is for the care of one or more new-born or adopted children as a result of a single pregnancy or placement`)
    THEN 15
    ELSE CONSIDER `the election made under section 152.05`
         WHEN `the 35-week maximum` THEN IF `the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with section 152.05` THEN 40 ELSE 35
         WHEN `the 61-week maximum` THEN IF `the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with section 152.05` THEN 69 ELSE 61

-- Subsection (3): two or more children placed for adoption at the same or substantially the same time are a single placement.
-- src:2498 | (3) For the purposes of this Part, the placement with a self-employed person, at the same or substantially the same time, of two or more children for the purpose of adoption is to be regarded as a single placement of a child or children for the purpose of adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(3) (src:2498)
GIVEN `two or more children are placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are placed at the same or substantially the same time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.14(3) the placements are regarded as a single placement of a child or children for the purpose of adoption` IF
        `two or more children are placed with the self-employed person for the purpose of adoption`
    AND `they are placed at the same or substantially the same time`

-- Subsections (5), (5.1) and (5.2): even if more than one claim is made, or more than one certificate issued, for the same
-- reason and the same family member (critically ill child, adult), the most weeks payable under the Act in respect of that
-- person is 26 (35, 15) in the 52 weeks that begin on the first day of the week of s 152.06(3)(a) (152.061(3)(a), 152.062(3)(a)).
-- src:2504 | (5) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 152.06 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 152.06 — for the same reason and in respect of the same family member, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that family member is 26 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.06(3)(a).
-- src:2506 | (5.1) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 152.061 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 152.061 — for the same reason and in respect of the same critically ill child, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that child is 35 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.061(3)(a).
-- src:2508 | (5.2) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 152.062 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 152.062 — for the same reason and in respect of the same critically ill adult, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that adult is 15 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.062(3)(a).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(5), (5.1), (5.2) (src:2504) (src:2506) (src:2508)
GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for benefits`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.14(5), (5.1) and (5.2) the maximum number of weeks of benefits in respect of one family member, critically ill child or critically ill adult` IS
    CONSIDER reason
    WHEN `care or support of a family member` THEN JUST 26
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill child` THEN JUST 35
    WHEN `care or support of a critically ill adult` THEN JUST 15
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Subsection (6): if a shorter period is prescribed for s 152.06(4), it takes the place of the 52 weeks in (5). The period
-- begins on the first day of the week in s 152.06(3)(a).
-- src:2504 | (5) Even if more than one claim is made under this Act, at least one of which is made under section 152.06 — or even if more than one certificate is issued for the purposes of this Act, at least one of which is issued for the purposes of section 152.06 — for the same reason and in respect of the same family member, the maximum number of weeks of benefits payable under this Act in respect of that family member is 26 weeks during the period of 52 weeks that begins on the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.06(3)(a).
-- src:2510 | (6) If a shorter period is prescribed for the purposes of subsection 152.06(4), then that shorter period applies for the purposes of subsection (5).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(5) and (6) (src:2504) (src:2510)
GIVEN `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.06(3)(a)` IS A DATE
      `the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of subsection 152.06(4), in weeks, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.06(4); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `ss 152.14(5) and (6) the period during which the maximum applies` IS
    `Period of days` OF `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.06(3)(a)`,
                        `the first day of the week referred to in paragraph 152.06(3)(a)` PLUS ((`weeks as days` `the number of weeks in the period`) MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the number of weeks in the period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the shorter period prescribed for the purposes of subsection 152.06(4), in weeks, if one is prescribed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 52
            WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- Subsection (7): when a shorter period of (6) has expired in respect of a family member, no further benefits are payable under
-- s 152.06 in respect of that family member until the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed.
-- src:2512 | (7) When a shorter period referred to in subsection (6) has expired in respect of a family member, no further benefits are payable under section 152.06 in respect of that family member until the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(7) (src:2512)
GIVEN `the shorter period has expired in respect of the family member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: s 152.14(7); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.14(7) no further benefits are payable under section 152.06 in respect of the family member` IF
        `the shorter period has expired in respect of the family member`
    AND NOT (`the minimum prescribed number of weeks has elapsed`)

-- Subsection (8): in a benefit period the person may combine the weeks of the several reasons, subject to the applicable
-- maximums, up to 50 combined weeks; if the benefit period is extended under s 152.11(14), up to the weeks of the maximum
-- benefit period calculated under s 152.11(16) less two.
-- src:2514 | (8) In a self-employed person’s benefit period, the self-employed person may, subject to the applicable maximums, combine weeks of benefits to which they are entitled because of a reason mentioned in subsection (1), but the maximum number of combined weeks is 50. However, if the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14), the maximum number of combined weeks equals the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16) less two weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(8) (src:2514)
GIVEN `the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.14(8) the maximum number of combined weeks` IS
    IF `the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14)`
    THEN `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks` MINUS 2
    ELSE 50

-- src:2514 | (8) In a self-employed person’s benefit period, the self-employed person may, subject to the applicable maximums, combine weeks of benefits to which they are entitled because of a reason mentioned in subsection (1), but the maximum number of combined weeks is 50. However, if the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14), the maximum number of combined weeks equals the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16) less two weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.14(8) (src:2514)
GIVEN `the number of combined weeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.14(8) the combined weeks are within the maximum` IF
    `the number of combined weeks` AT MOST `s 152.14(8) the maximum number of combined weeks` `the benefit period is extended under subsection 152.11(14)` `the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 152.11(16), in weeks`

§ `152.15 Waiting period`

-- "waiting period means the one week of the benefit period described in section 152.15" (s 152.01(1)).
-- src:2516 | 152.15 A self-employed person is not entitled to be paid benefits in a benefit period until, after the beginning of the benefit period, the person has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.15 (src:2516)
`s 152.15 the waiting period of a self-employed person, in weeks` MEANS 1

-- A person is not entitled to be paid benefits in a benefit period until, after the beginning of the benefit period, they
-- have served a waiting period of one week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
-- src:2516 | 152.15 A self-employed person is not entitled to be paid benefits in a benefit period until, after the beginning of the benefit period, the person has served a waiting period of one week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.15 (src:2516)
GIVEN `the number of weeks of unemployment, after the beginning of the benefit period, for which benefits would otherwise be payable, that the person has served as waiting period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.15 the person has served the waiting period and is entitled to be paid benefits` IF
    `the number of weeks of unemployment, after the beginning of the benefit period, for which benefits would otherwise be payable, that the person has served as waiting period` AT LEAST `s 152.15 the waiting period of a self-employed person, in weeks`

-- Section 152.151(1): for determining the waiting period, a week of unemployment is deemed to be a week for which benefits
-- would otherwise be payable if, were the week not the waiting period, the benefits payable in that week after deducting (a) the
-- earnings greater than $50, when the weekly rate is less than $200, or (b) the earnings greater than 25% of the weekly rate,
-- when it is $200 or more, would be greater than zero. By (2) the deduction of s 152.18(2) is left out of the benefits that
-- would have been payable, and the earnings are those of s 152.18(2).
-- src:2518 | 152.151 (1) For the purpose of determining a self-employed person’s waiting period, a week of unemployment is deemed to be a week of unemployment for which benefits would otherwise be payable if — were the week not the waiting period — the amount of the benefits that would have been payable in that week after deducting the following would be greater than zero:
-- src:2519 | (a) the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than $50, if the person’s rate of weekly benefits is less than $200; or
-- src:2520 | (b) the amount of the earnings, if any, that is greater than 25% of the person’s rate of weekly benefits, if that rate is $200 or more.
-- src:2521 | References
-- src:2522 | (2) For the purpose of subsection (1),
-- src:2523 | (a) in determining the amount of the benefits that would have been payable, the deduction referred to in subsection 152.18(2) is to be excluded; and
-- src:2524 | (b) a reference to earnings means earnings as determined for the purpose of subsection 152.18(2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.151 (src:2518-2524)
GIVEN `the person's rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the earnings of the week` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.151(1) the week of unemployment is deemed to be a week for which benefits would otherwise be payable` IF
    `the person's rate of weekly benefits` MINUS `the part of the earnings that is deducted` GREATER THAN 0
    WHERE
        `the amount of earnings that is not deducted` MEANS
            IF `the person's rate of weekly benefits` LESS THAN 200
            THEN 50
            ELSE `the person's rate of weekly benefits` TIMES 25%
        `the part of the earnings that is deducted` MEANS
            max 0 (`the earnings of the week` MINUS `the amount of earnings that is not deducted`)

§ `152.16 and 152.17 Rate of weekly benefits`

-- Subsection (2) (and (2.1) of s 152.18): only the part of the aggregate of the amounts of s 152.16(1)(a) and (b) that does not
-- exceed the maximum yearly insurable earnings as calculated under section 4 is taken into account.
-- src:2530 | (2) Only the portion of the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) that does not exceed the maximum yearly insurable earnings as calculated under section 4 is to be taken into account for the purposes of subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.16(2) (src:2530)
GIVEN `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER   -- keel: eia-core-maximum-earnings; the published figure is an input
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.16(2) and 152.18(2.1) the part of the aggregate taken into account` IS
    min `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`

-- Subsection (1): the rate is 55% (33% for the weeks for which the person is paid benefits under s 152.05 where the
-- applicable maximum is the 61 weeks of s 152.14(1)(b)(ii)) of the result of dividing the aggregate of (a) the self-employed
-- earnings of the qualifying period (as s 152.01(2) determines them) and (b) the insurable earnings from employment of the
-- qualifying period (calculated without the prescribed insurable earnings: reg 24.3, piece er2) by 52, the aggregate being
-- held to the maximum yearly insurable earnings by (2). Rounded to the nearest dollar by s 152.01(5).
-- src:2526 | 152.16 (1) The rate of weekly benefits payable to a self-employed person is 55% — or 33% for the weeks for which the self-employed person is paid benefits under section 152.05 in the case where the applicable maximum number of weeks is established in subparagraph 152.14(1)(b)(ii) — of the result obtained by dividing the aggregate of the amounts referred to in the following paragraphs (a) and (b) by 52:
-- src:2527 | (a) the amount of their self-employed earnings, determined under paragraph 152.01(2)(a), (b) or (c), as the case may be, for their qualifying period; and
-- src:2528 | (b) if they had insurable earnings from employment, including insurable earnings earned as a person to whom regulations made under Part VIII apply, for their qualifying period, the amount of those insurable earnings for that period, calculated without taking into account prescribed insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.16(1) (src:2526-2528)
GIVEN `the person's self-employed earnings for the qualifying period` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's insurable earnings from employment for the qualifying period, calculated without taking into account prescribed insurable earnings` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 24.3 (piece er2)
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the week is a week for which benefits are paid under section 152.05` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election made under section 152.05` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.16(1) the rate of weekly benefits payable to a self-employed person` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar`
        (`the percentage` TIMES (`ss 152.16(2) and 152.18(2.1) the part of the aggregate taken into account` `the aggregate of the two amounts` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`) DIVIDED BY 52)
    WHERE
        `the aggregate of the two amounts` MEANS
            `the person's self-employed earnings for the qualifying period` PLUS `the person's insurable earnings from employment for the qualifying period, calculated without taking into account prescribed insurable earnings`
        `the percentage` MEANS
            IF `the week is a week for which benefits are paid under section 152.05` AND `the election made under section 152.05` EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
            THEN 33%
            ELSE 55%

-- Section 152.17: the rate of a person with one or more dependent children is increased by the family supplement determined
-- in accordance with the regulations (reg 34, piece er2) if the person establishes, in the manner the Commission directs, that
-- they meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria.
-- src:2532 | 152.17 (1) The rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person who has one or more dependent children shall be increased by the amount of a family supplement determined in accordance with the regulations if the person establishes, in the manner that the Commission may direct, that the person meets the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.17(1) (src:2532)
GIVEN `the person has one or more dependent children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person establishes, in the manner the Commission may direct, that they meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: reg 34 (piece er2)
      `the family supplement determined in accordance with the regulations` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 34 (piece er2)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.17(1) the family supplement by which the rate is increased` IS
    IF `the person has one or more dependent children` AND `the person establishes, in the manner the Commission may direct, that they meet the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria`
    THEN `the family supplement determined in accordance with the regulations`
    ELSE 0

-- Subsections (2) and (3): the criteria "may include" those of the Canada child benefit, which is a deemed overpayment under the
-- Income Tax Act. A power of the regulations; nothing for the person to state beyond the criteria (reg 34).

-- Subsection (4): the increase must not exceed the prescribed percentage of the person's self-employed earnings for the year
-- divided by 52 or, if none is prescribed, 25%.
-- src:2538 | (4) The amount of the increase in the self-employed person’s rate of weekly benefits shall not exceed the prescribed percentage of their amount of self-employed earnings for the year divided by 52 or, if no percentage is prescribed, 25%.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.17(4) (src:2538)
GIVEN `the person's amount of self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed percentage, if one is prescribed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   -- out of range: s 152.17(4); none found in the Regulations
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.17(4) the greatest increase in the rate of weekly benefits` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the percentage` TIMES `the person's amount of self-employed earnings for the year` DIVIDED BY 52)
    WHERE
        `the percentage` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the prescribed percentage, if one is prescribed`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 25%
            WHEN JUST p THEN p

-- Subsection (5): the maximum rate of weekly benefits is 55% of the maximum yearly insurable earnings, as calculated under
-- s 4, divided by 52.
-- src:2540 | (5) The maximum rate of weekly benefits that may be paid under this section is 55% of the maximum yearly insurable earnings, as calculated under section 4, divided by 52.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.17(5) (src:2540)
GIVEN `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.17(5) the maximum rate of weekly benefits` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (55% TIMES `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` DIVIDED BY 52)

-- The rate with the supplement: the rate plus the supplement (itself held to the greatest increase of (4)), held to the maximum rate.
-- src:2532 | 152.17 (1) The rate of weekly benefits of a self-employed person who has one or more dependent children shall be increased by the amount of a family supplement determined in accordance with the regulations if the person establishes, in the manner that the Commission may direct, that the person meets the prescribed low-income family eligibility criteria.
-- src:2538 | (4) The amount of the increase in the self-employed person’s rate of weekly benefits shall not exceed the prescribed percentage of their amount of self-employed earnings for the year divided by 52 or, if no percentage is prescribed, 25%.
-- src:2540 | (5) The maximum rate of weekly benefits that may be paid under this section is 55% of the maximum yearly insurable earnings, as calculated under section 4, divided by 52.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.17(1), (4) and (5) (src:2532) (src:2538) (src:2540)
GIVEN `the rate of weekly benefits under section 152.16` IS A NUMBER
      `the family supplement by which the rate is increased` IS A NUMBER
      `the greatest increase in the rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum rate of weekly benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.17 the rate of weekly benefits with the family supplement` IS
    min (`the rate of weekly benefits under section 152.16` PLUS (min `the family supplement by which the rate is increased` `the greatest increase in the rate of weekly benefits`))
        `the maximum rate of weekly benefits`

§ `152.18 and 152.19 Deductions`

-- Subsection (1): earnings during the waiting period: an amount not exceeding those earnings is deducted, as prescribed
-- (reg 39(1), piece er3), from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
-- src:2542 | 152.18 (1) If a self-employed person has earnings during their waiting period, an amount not exceeding those earnings shall, as prescribed, be deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits would otherwise be payable.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.18(1) (src:2542)
GIVEN `the earnings during the waiting period` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the regulations prescribe to be deducted` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: reg 39(1) (piece er3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.18(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks` IS
    min `the amount the regulations prescribe to be deducted` `the earnings during the waiting period`

-- Subsection (2): for earnings in any other week of unemployment the deduction is the total of 50% of the earnings that are
-- at most 90% of the result of dividing the aggregate of s 152.16(1)(a) and (b) (held to the maximum by (2.1)) by 52, and
-- 100% of the earnings above that. Subject to ss 152.03(3), 152.04(4) and (3). Rounded to the nearest dollar by s 152.01(5).
-- src:2544 | (2) Subject to subsections (3), 152.03(3) and 152.04(4), if the self-employed person has earnings during any other week of unemployment, there shall be deducted from benefits payable in that week the amount equal to the total of
-- src:2545 | (a) 50% of the earnings that are less than or equal to 90% of the result obtained by dividing the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52, and
-- src:2546 | (b) 100% of the earnings that are greater than 90% of the result obtained by dividing the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) by 52.
-- src:2547 | Excess not to be included
-- src:2548 | (2.1) Only the portion of the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b) that does not exceed the maximum yearly insurable earnings as calculated under section 4 is to be taken into account for the purpose of subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.18(2) and (2.1) (src:2544-2548)
GIVEN `the earnings of the week` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.18(2) the deduction for earnings in a week of unemployment` IS
    `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar`
        (50% TIMES (min `the earnings of the week` `ninety per cent of the weekly figure`)
         PLUS 100% TIMES (max 0 (`the earnings of the week` MINUS `ninety per cent of the weekly figure`)))
    WHERE
        `ninety per cent of the weekly figure` MEANS
            90% TIMES (`ss 152.16(2) and 152.18(2.1) the part of the aggregate taken into account` `the aggregate of the amounts referred to in paragraphs 152.16(1)(a) and (b)` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`) DIVIDED BY 52

-- Subsection (3)(a): the person failed to declare earnings: the amount deducted from the benefits paid for the period is (i) the
-- undeclared earnings if, in the Commission's opinion, the person knowingly failed to declare them; (ii) otherwise the
-- undeclared earnings less the difference between (A) all amounts determined under (2)(a) or (b) for the period and (B) all
-- amounts applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period.
-- src:2549 | Undeclared earnings
-- src:2550 | (3) If the self-employed person has failed to declare all or some of their earnings to the Commission for a period, determined under the regulations, for which benefits were claimed,
-- src:2551 | (a) the following amount shall be deducted from the benefits paid to the person for that period:
-- src:2552 | (i) the amount of the undeclared earnings, if, in the opinion of the Commission, the person knowingly failed to declare the earnings, or
-- src:2553 | (ii) in any other case, the amount of the undeclared earnings less the difference between
-- src:2554 | (A) all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period,
-- src:2555 | and
-- src:2556 | (B) all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.18(3)(a) (src:2549-2556)
GIVEN `the amount of the undeclared earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `in the opinion of the Commission, the person knowingly failed to declare the earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period` IS A NUMBER
      `all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.18(3)(a) the amount to be deducted for undeclared earnings` IS
    IF `in the opinion of the Commission, the person knowingly failed to declare the earnings`
    THEN `the amount of the undeclared earnings`
    ELSE max 0 (`the amount of the undeclared earnings`
                  MINUS (`all amounts determined under paragraph (2)(a) or (b) for the period` MINUS `all amounts that were applied under those paragraphs in respect of the declared earnings for the period`))

-- Subsection (3)(b): the deduction is made from the benefits paid for a number of weeks beginning with the first week for which
-- the earnings were not declared, so that the amount deducted in each consecutive week equals the person's benefits paid for
-- that week. The last week takes only what remains (fork F21). The list is the benefits paid week by week.
-- src:2557 | (b) the deduction shall be made
-- src:2558 | (i) from the benefits paid for a number of weeks that begins with the first week for which the earnings were not declared in that period, and
-- src:2559 | (ii) in such a manner that the amount deducted in each consecutive week equals the person’s benefits paid for that week.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.18(3)(b) (src:2557-2559)
GIVEN `the amount still to be deducted` IS A NUMBER
      `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, beginning with the first week for which the earnings were not declared` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `s 152.18(3)(b) the amounts deducted in consecutive weeks` IS
    IF `the amount still to be deducted` AT MOST 0 OR null `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, beginning with the first week for which the earnings were not declared`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE `the amount deducted in the first week` FOLLOWED BY
         `s 152.18(3)(b) the amounts deducted in consecutive weeks`
             (`the amount still to be deducted` MINUS `the amount deducted in the first week`)
             (drop 1 `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, beginning with the first week for which the earnings were not declared`)
    WHERE
        `the amount deducted in the first week` MEANS
            min `the amount still to be deducted` (at `the benefits paid for each consecutive week, beginning with the first week for which the earnings were not declared` 0)

-- Section 152.19(1) and (2): for each working day (reg 32: any day but Saturday and Sunday) on which the person is not
-- entitled to receive benefits, in the waiting period (1) or, being disentitled, in another week of unemployment (2), an amount
-- equal to 1/5 of the weekly rate is deducted: from the benefits payable for the three weeks of s 152.18(1) (1) or for that
-- week (2). One fifth of the rate is rounded to the nearest dollar (s 152.01(5)).
-- src:2561 | 152.19 (1) If a self-employed person is not entitled to receive benefits for a working day in their waiting period, an amount equal to 1/5 of their weekly rate of benefits for each such working day shall be deducted from the benefits payable for the three weeks described in subsection 152.18(1).
-- src:2563 | (2) If a self-employed person is disentitled from receiving benefits for a working day in a week of unemployment that is not in their waiting period, an amount equal to 1/5 of their weekly rate of benefits for each such working day shall be deducted from the benefits payable for that week.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.19(1) and (2) (src:2561) (src:2563)
GIVEN `the person's weekly rate of benefits` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of working days on which the person is not entitled to receive benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ss 152.19(1) and (2) the deduction for working days on which the person is not entitled` IS
    `the number of working days on which the person is not entitled to receive benefits`
        TIMES `s 6(2) and s 152.01(5) amount rounded to the nearest dollar` (`the person's weekly rate of benefits` DIVIDED BY 5)

§ `152.2 Prison inmates and persons outside Canada`

-- Except as may otherwise be prescribed (regs 54 and 55.01, piece er3), a self-employed person is not entitled to receive
-- benefits for any period during which they are an inmate of a prison or similar institution or are not in Canada.
-- src:2565 | 152.2 Except as may otherwise be prescribed, a self-employed person is not entitled to receive benefits for any period during which the person
-- src:2566 | (a) is an inmate of a prison or similar institution; or
-- src:2567 | (b) is not in Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 152.2 (src:2565-2567)
GIVEN `the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation otherwise provides for the person's case` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: regs 54(2) and 55.01 (piece er3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 152.2 the person is not entitled to receive benefits for the period` IF
        (`the person is an inmate of a prison or similar institution` OR `the person is not in Canada`)
    AND NOT (`a regulation otherwise provides for the person's case`)
